         and \eqn{N} is the total number of choices. The index is then
         transformed back to an effective-size scale:
         \deqn{E' = \frac{1}{1-I} = \frac{N^2}{\sum_i o_i^2}
         = \frac{1}{\sum_i p_i^2}.}
         This formula is algebraically equivalent to a reciprocal
         concentration form.
